WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:19.000
A stroke occurs when the blood flow in part of your brain is blocked.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.260
After just a few minutes, the starved brain
cells begin to die.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.380
Normally, the brain receives blood via two
major pairs of arteries,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.960
which branch throughout brain tissue,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.840
and supply your brain cells with
a constant flow of oxygen, glucose, and nutrients

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.060
necessary for their functions.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.000
In one type of stroke, ischemic stroke,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.337
an artery in your brain narrows,

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:17.000
or becomes completely blocked, preventing normal blood flow.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.040
The blockage may be caused by a blood clot, also called a thrombus,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.120
which forms in an unhealthy
artery of the brain.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The lack of blood flow causes the tissue the artery supplies to become starved, or ischemic.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:45.220
Similarly, the blockage may be due to an embolus,
a blood clot that forms elsewhere in the body

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.240
and travels to the brain.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.620
The embolus lodges in a narrow artery and obstructs blood flow.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.400
In contrast, during a hemorrhagic stroke,

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.580
abnormal bleeding disrupts normal blood flow.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:21.680
For example, in an intracerebral hemorrhagic stroke,

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.460
a blood vessel bursts, spilling blood directly onto your brain,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.100
while robbing the intended tissue of nourishment.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.700
Both the hemorrhage and ischemia destroy brain tissue.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.738
A subarachnoid hemorrhagic stroke

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:50.480
occurs when a weak spot in a blood vessel wall, called an aneurysm, bursts

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.140
and leaks blood into the tight space between your brain and your skull.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:03.200
The high-pressure bleeding results in serious damage to brain tissue.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Immediate treatment for your stroke may help
to minimize brain cell injury and death.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.620
If you have an ischemic stroke,

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.940
you may be given medication to break up the clot causing your stroke.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.600
Later, your doctor may recommend surgery,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.680
such as carotid endarterectomy, to reduce your risk of having another ischemic stroke.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.640
In the case of hemorrhagic stroke,

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.580
emergency surgery may be necessary

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.900
to repair damaged arteries,

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.520
or reduce the pressure of the blood on your brain.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:05.460
You may be given medication to help the brain’s blood flow return to normal.

